  {
   "id": 3514,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1420,
    -700
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    380
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 21,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "H3 CLIP PLAN - GENERATION, FREE MODE (sound generated by H3)\n\nExample: copy the files of the plugin's examples/ folder into ComfyUI/input/ (robot_workshop.plan.json, robot.png, workshop.png). This workflow is already set up for them.\n\n1. Pick the plan in 'H3 Plan - Clip' (list, or button 'choose plan file' / drag and drop). The plan must contain \"mode\": \"free\". There is no song in this workflow.\n2. Images: one 'REF' node per image (name = the name in the plan).\n3. Voices: one 'VOICE' node per character, with the SAME name as its image (or a name of its own for an off-screen character). Pick the file in the list, with the 'choose audio file' button or by drag and drop (copied to input/voices). Clean sample of 2 to 15 s; beyond 15 s in total per clip, each voice is cut. Without a VOICE node for a character, H3 picks its voice. At most 3 voices per clip. The 'VOICE robot' node is bypassed: to give the robot a voice, choose a sample and un-bypass it (Ctrl+B).\n4. Choose the resolution, set clip_index to 1 on 'increment', set the run count to the number of clips, run.\n\nEach clip's preview has the sound generated by H3. A 'continue' clip takes over the end (picture AND sound) of the previous clip on disk: redo the 'continue' clips that follow a changed clip too.\nAssembly: workflow '2 Assemble (free)'."
   ],
   "title": "How to use"
  },
